  <lyrics>
    <verse name="v1">
      <lines>
      <chord name="C"/>For <chord name="Dm7"/>sun<chord name="G"/>rise <chord name="C"/>hope and <chord name="Dm7"/>sun<chord name="G"/>set <chord name="C"/>calm,<br/>
      And <chord name="Fsus"/>all<chord name="Dm7"/>that <chord name="Gsus7"/>lies<chord name="G"/>be<chord name="C"/>tw<chord name="Dm7"/>een,<chord name="C"/><br/>
      For <chord name="Dm7"/>all <chord name="G"/>the <chord name="C"/>sweetness <chord name="Dm7"/>and <chord name="G"/>the <chord name="C"/>balm<br/>
      That <chord name="Fsus"/>is<chord name="Dm7"/>and <chord name="Gsus7"/>that<chord name="G"/>has <chord name="C"/>be<chord name="Dm7"/>en,<chord name="C"/><br/>
      <chord name="C"/>For <chord name="G"/>comrade<chord name="Am7"/>ship <chord name="D"/>for <chord name="G"/>peace in <chord name="Am7"/>strife,<br/>
      <chord name="D"/>And <chord name="G"/>light on <chord name="Am7"/>dark<chord name="D7"/>ened <chord name="G"/>da<chord name="G7"/>ys;<chord name="C"/><br/>
      <chord name="G7"/>For <chord name="C"/>work to <chord name="Dm7"/>do<chord name="G"/>and <chord name="C"/>strength for <chord name="Dm7"/>life<br/>
      <chord name="G"/>We <chord name="C"/>sing our <chord name="Dm7"/>hymn <chord name="G"/>of <chord name="C"/>praise.
      </lines>
    </verse>
    <verse name="v2">
      <lines>
      <chord name="C"/>But <chord name="Dm7"/>O, we <chord name="G"/>press far, <chord name="C"/>far <chord name="Dm7"/>above these <chord name="G"/>gifts of <chord name="C"/>pure delight,<br/>
      <chord name="Fsus"/>And <chord name="Dm7"/>find <chord name="Gsus7"/>in Thee, <chord name="G"/>and <chord name="C"/>in Thy <chord name="Dm7"/>love <chord name="C"/>contentment infinite.<br/>
      <chord name="Dm7"/>O Lord, <chord name="G"/>beloved, in <chord name="C"/>whom are <chord name="Dm7"/>found all <chord name="G"/>joys of <chord name="C"/>time and place,<br/>
      <chord name="Fsus"/>What <chord name="Dm7"/>will it <chord name="Gsus7"/>be when <chord name="G"/>joy is <chord name="C"/>crowned by <chord name="Dm7"/>vision of <chord name="C"/>Thy face?
